## Integration with Existing Systems

### Archive system
- The Queue feature uses the existing archive functionality.
- When confirmation modal's "Archive Videos" is clicked, each watched video is archived using the same code path that the existing X-on-thumbnail archive button uses.
- Archived videos follow the existing 14-day cleanup behavior.

### YouTube API
- The Queue feature does NOT make any new API calls.
- It only uses already-fetched video data (snippet, duration, thumbnail) stored from the existing fetch cycle.
- All player embedding uses the IFrame Player API, which is free and separate from the Data API quota.

### Substack section
- No changes.

### Settings modal
- No changes.

### Dark / light mode
- All new UI elements (queue icon, badge, modal, player section, queue panel, confirmation modals, undo toast) must support both themes consistently with the rest of the dashboard.

### Refresh button
- The refresh button continues to work as before.
- It should NOT clear the queue or change its state.
- Note: when refresh is clicked, archived videos are removed from the dashboard view. Watched-but-not-yet-archived videos in the queue remain accessible (this is the whole point of the two-stage model).

