## Implementation Approach (Suggested)

Recommend implementing in **two passes** to make testing manageable:

### Pass 1: Queue infrastructure (no player)
- localStorage data model and helper functions (add, remove, reorder, clear, toggle watched, etc.)
- Queue icon button on thumbnails (both states)
- A dedicated `updateQueueIcons()` function that walks all `.content-card` elements in the DOM and updates only the queue badge on each card (position number, green state, hidden state) without calling `renderVideos()`. This is necessary because `renderVideos()` uses `innerHTML` bulk re-rendering, which would reset scroll position on every queue change. `updateQueueIcons()` should be called any time the queue array changes (add, remove, reorder).
- Queue badge in YouTube section header
- Queue modal
- Clear All with undo toast (without confirmation modal yet, since nothing is "watched" without the player)
- Dark mode support for all of the above
- Test: user can build, view, reorder, and remove queue items. State persists across reloads.

### Pass 2: Player and session logic
- IFrame Player API integration
- Player section
- Queue panel below player (with current-video highlight)
- Playback tracking and 90% threshold logic
- Auto-advance
- Previous / Next / Archive / Close controls
- Watch Again button on grayed items
- Session-end and Queue-complete confirmation modals
- Wire up Clear All to use confirmation modal when watched videos exist
- Test: full flow including stepping-away scenarios.

